\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Judge validation on all English responses. The refusal judge is compared with an LLM-free string-match refusal detector; the content judge is compared with the official \textsc  {HarmBench}\xspace  classifier. The content judge recovers 79--99\% of \textsc  {HarmBench}\xspace  -positive completions but also counts vague or non-harmful attempts, which is why we report the \textsc  {HarmBench}\xspace  rate as the stricter harmful-compliance measure.\relax }}{16}{table.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:judge}{{9}{16}{Judge validation on all English responses. The refusal judge is compared with an LLM-free string-match refusal detector; the content judge is compared with the official \harmbench classifier. The content judge recovers 79--99\% of \harmbench -positive completions but also counts vague or non-harmful attempts, which is why we report the \harmbench rate as the stricter harmful-compliance measure.\relax }{table.caption.16}{}}
